 {"$schema":"fabro-journal-v1","run_id":"01M1XN2KWG6T0PHRTJWZ8R0AZX","node":"implementer","visit":1,"status":"succeeded","ts":"2026-09-07T10:33:00Z","data":{"painpoints":[{"text":"TestAppStateBuilder (lib/apps/fabro-server/src/test_support.rs) had no github_api_base_url setter until this seed added one — every it-test needing a mock GitHub had to either stay in the cfg(test) unit suite or duplicate create_github_token_app_state (fabro-bde4, run 01M1XN2KWG6T0PHRTJWZ8R0AZX). Suggestion: consider exposing a shared mock-github app helper in test_support so future it-tests don't re-derive the token-strategy settings + vault_entries incantation."}],"observations":["httpmock 0.8.3 has no per-mock hit limit (no up_to_n_times); modeling transient-then-changed GitHub responses requires spawning the request task, waiting on mock.calls_async(), then mock.delete() + creating the follow-up mock — the pattern used in merged_wait_ignores_transient_blocked_observation.","wait.rs uses std::time::Instant for the poll cadence, so paused-clock tokio tests cannot fast-forward it; the confirmation interval (BLOCKED_CONFIRMATION_POLL_INTERVAL=1.5s) is what keeps sustained-window tests fast rather than 10s+ (GITHUB_POLL_INTERVAL)."]}}
